  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 948 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nLighter winds are forecast for today as the upper trough moves\nfurther east into the Midwest and sfc high pressure settles in.\nOther than a few high clouds, mainly clear skies and cool temps\ntoday (5-10 degrees below normal). \n\nA shortwave trough swings by to the north Wed PM, generating a\nmodest pressure gradient and lee troughing to the east. W-SW\nwinds of 10-15 mph are forecast with gusts to 25-30 in the \nafternoon. Higher gusts are expected in the Sacs, but remaining\nbelow advisory criteria. Any rain chances associated with the\ndisturbance stay far to the north. Zonal flow for Thu behind the\nshortwave keeps us mainly clear with light winds returning. \n\nA baggy upper trough moves into the Desert SW late this week, \nbringing some moisture and cloud cover to the region Fri/Sat. Rain\nchances are limited as PWs climb to only 0.5-0.6\". Some diffluent\nflow may try to form a few showers, but any impacts will be \nnegligible through Sat with limited instability. This weak trough\nlooks to become cut-off from the flow early next week off the Baja\ncoast with most impacts over AZ in terms of rain chances. \nConfidence is low in any chance of rain for us through next Tue. \nAs of now, increased cloud cover can be expected late in the \nperiod. If enough moisture reaches NM, western areas would be most\nlikely to see rain.\n\nTemps remain near or just below average into next week with \nlowland highs in the mid 60s to low 70s most days. Other than \nbreeziness on Wed, winds will be generally light.",
